# G8 Flow — Brand

Brand name / logo / credentials: **G8 Flow**.

## Colors (strict usage mix)

| Token | Hex | Site usage |
|-------|-----|------------|
| `--g8-navy` | `#08163C` | ~60% — primary surfaces, hero fields, deep backgrounds |
| `--g8-blue` | `#15389B` | ~30% — accents, links, secondary fills, CTAs (with navy) |
| `--g8-forest` | `#264238` | ~10% — rare accent / grounding / secondary detail |

Use a navy→blue gradient (`#08163C` → `#15389B`) as the dominant atmospheric field. Do not invent purple/indigo AI-default themes. Do not use cream+terracotta or newspaper layouts.

## Typography (Flux scale; Satoshi substitute)

Source site: https://www.flux-academy.com/ — Flux uses **Britti Sans** (commercial). This project uses **Satoshi** unless Britti is licensed later. Details: `docs/g8-flow/content/typography.md`.

- Family: `Satoshi`, fallbacks `Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif`
- Body: ~1rem, line-height ~1.5, letter-spacing ~0.03rem
- H1 desktop ~4.5rem / lh ~4.8rem; large desktop ~5.5rem; tablet ~3.5rem; mobile ~2.75rem
- H2 desktop ~4rem; H3 ~3.5rem; H4 ~3rem; H5 ~2rem; H6 ~1.5rem
- Headings: weight 600; sentence case OK when Hormozi clarity needs it
- Do not use Inter/Roboto as the brand face

## Visual direction

- Premium, futuristic, Awwwards / Apple-adjacent motion — not noisy
- Full-bleed hero media; no inset hero cards; no floating promo chips on hero imagery
- One composition per first viewport; brand/name is a hero-level signal
- Prefer expressive type (Britti) over Inter/Roboto/system defaults
- Atmosphere via navy/blue gradient + imagery; avoid flat single-color pages
